orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NIkhilSaravade/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NIkhilSaravade/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NIkhilSaravade/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NIkhilSaravade/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NIkhilSaravade","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/commits/d4c1deea09b48c771dd80775d7ad2fa081f07b4e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T10:54:33Z","email":"90844573+NIkhilSaravade@users.noreply.github.com","name":"NIkhilSaravade"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T10:54:33Z","email":"90844573+NIkhilSaravade@users.noreply.github.com","name":"NIkhilSaravade"},"message":"Phase B follow-ups: real comparison, explain hardening, frontend surfacing\n\n1. scripts/compare_explain_vs_review.py - a real, committed side-by-side\n   comparison of the explain and review prompts, closing the gap the\n   original Phase B build-log entry disclosed (the scratch comparison\n   crashed on a missing local pgvector extension). Reuses\n   evals/run_eval.py''s existing RAG-stub pattern instead of modifying\n   the shared local Postgres install - real Groq output on both sides,\n   real BM25 grounding, no live vector search needed. Real captured\n   output in results/explain_vs_review_comparison.json: 749 chars of\n   terse review JSON vs. 3,643 chars of pedagogical explain prose.\n\n2. Explain hardening: a new ExplanationGenerationFailed exception,\n   raised when the LLM returns an empty response, mapped to a 502 -\n   mirrors AnalysisOutputInvalid''s \"never cache a bad result\" rule,\n   applied to explain''s own content-addressed cache. Plus a test\n   confirming an empty RAG context doesn''t crash prompt formatting.\n\n3. Frontend: SolvePage.tsx''s Result tab now surfaces an \"Explain this\n   solution\" banner right after a real, judged PASSED Submit (not a\n   mere Run), wired to hand the just-finished submissionId directly to\n   handleExplain to avoid a race with the async pastSubmissions\n   refresh.\n\nBackend: 98 passed, 3 deselected (was 82), ruff clean. Frontend:\ntsc/oxlint/build clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"78717a65770f0b2cce5239edbcbcc3520fa03c00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/git/trees/78717a65770f0b2cce5239edbcbcc3520fa03c00"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/git/commits/d4c1deea09b48c771dd80775d7ad2fa081f07b4e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90844573?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NIkhilSaravade/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NIkhilSaravade/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NIkhilSaravade/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NIkhilSaravade/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NIkhilSaravade","id":90844573,"login":"NIkhilSaravade","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwODQ0NTcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NIkhilSaravade/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NIkhilSaravade/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NIkhilSaravade/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NIkhilSaravade/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NIkhilSaravade/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NIkhilSaravade","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/commit/d4c1deea09b48c771dd80775d7ad2fa081f07b4e","node_id":"C_kwDORTK7XtoAKGQ0YzFkZWVhMDliNDhjNzcxZGQ4MDc3NWQ3YWQyZmEwODFmMDdiNGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/commit/eef735e54419770c29beb9724105dcb42bd7e96c","sha":"eef735e54419770c29beb9724105dcb42bd7e96c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/commits/eef735e54419770c29beb9724105dcb42bd7e96c"}],"sha":"d4c1deea09b48c771dd80775d7ad2fa081f07b4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/commits/d4c1deea09b48c771dd80775d7ad2fa081f07b4e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90844573?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NIkhilSaravade/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NIkhilSaravade/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NIkhilSaravade/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NIkhilSaravade/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NIkhilSaravade","id":90844573,"login":"NIkhilSaravade","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwODQ0NTcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NIkhilSaravade/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NIkhilSaravade/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NIkhilSaravade/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NIkhilSaravade/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NIkhilSaravade/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NIkhilSaravade","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/commits/eef735e54419770c29beb9724105dcb42bd7e96c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T10:45:02Z","email":"90844573+NIkhilSaravade@users.noreply.github.com","name":"NIkhilSaravade"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T10:45:02Z","email":"90844573+NIkhilSaravade@users.noreply.github.com","name":"NIkhilSaravade"},"message":"Fix known-limitations item 8: HintSession had no reset\n\nAdds an explicit POST /ai/hint/{problemId}/reset and an automatic\nreset on a fresh PASSED submission (wired into the existing\nanalysis.trigger.v1 Kafka consumer), both routing through the same\nservices.hint_service._start_new_attempt semantics. HintSession gains\nan attempt_number column that increments on reset instead of the row\nbeing replaced, so hint history stays queryable per attempt.\n\nDocumented double-reset behavior: a reset only bumps attempt_number\nwhen there''s actually something to reset (current_level > 0), so an\nexplicit reset and the automatic one landing back-to-back in either\norder increment attempt_number exactly once, never twice.\n\n27 new/updated tests (services/hint_service.py, a new\ntests/test_kafka_hint_reset.py exercising the real Kafka consumer\npath, and the reset endpoint''s HTTP wiring) all pass; full suite\n94 passed, 3 deselected. docs/ai-code-review-known-limitations.md\nitem 8''s reset bullet moved to resolved with the real test count -\nthe other two disclosed gaps in that item are untouched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e20f11197d8b9d1b3500758fa7f174693e526223","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/git/trees/e20f11197d8b9d1b3500758fa7f174693e526223"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/git/commits/eef735e54419770c29beb9724105dcb42bd7e96c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90844573?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NIkhilSaravade/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NIkhilSaravade/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NIkhilSaravade/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NIkhilSaravade/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NIkhilSaravade