d":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/commits/b538b9563f81e24f1f80311de9a8d3473760f852/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T19:05:40Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T19:05:40Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Right-size sandbox CPU quotas per language and trim platform CPU limits\n\nTwo changes aimed at maximizing safe concurrency on this single 4-vCPU\nnode, without adding risk of repeating the Go-style throttling failure:\n\n1. Per-language sandbox CPU quota tiers, extending the Go-only override\n   from the previous fix to every language:\n   - Python/JavaScript (pure interpretation, no compile step): 0.15\n   - Java/TypeScript (real compile step - javac/tsc): 0.5, as cheap\n     insurance against the same class of CFS-throttling failure Go hit,\n     since both were sitting at the same 0.3 quota that broke Go\n   - C/C++ stay on the 0.3 platform default (small native compiles are\n     cheap enough that no override is warranted)\n   - Go stays at 1.0 (unchanged from the previous fix)\n\n2. Trimmed platform-namespace CPU *limits* (not requests, which are\n   unchanged and still govern scheduling): auth-service, api-gateway,\n   submission-service, problem-service 750m->500m; ai-analysis-service,\n   execution-result-service 500m->400m; user-service, solution-service\n   500m->350m. discovery-service (most mesh-critical) and\n   worker-service-go (needs its full core under real load) are\n   unchanged. This drops platform-wide limits from 6700m to 5200m\n   (167%->130% of the node''s 4000m capacity) - it doesn''t change what\n   gets scheduled, but caps how far simultaneous bursts across services\n   can stack, which is what was driving the intermittent\n   Eureka/DNS-flakiness-under-load pattern (\"works, then randomly\n   doesn''t\") reported throughout today''s session.\n\nNo ConfigMap change needed for the sandbox quota tiers - all the new\ndefaults already apply.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0149o5QZBdtHxkX8gdsNfEwW","tree":{"sha":"2ef2722692d678efbef177ba3e0a2cb181a7bbea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/git/trees/2ef2722692d678efbef177ba3e0a2cb181a7bbea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/git/commits/b538b9563f81e24f1f80311de9a8d3473760f852","verification":{"payload":"tree 2ef2722692d678efbef177ba3e0a2cb181a7bbea\nparent ac1bc14886c4a9d6486e27b90dbfdfd151acaeba\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1788721540 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1788721540 +0000\n\nRight-size sandbox CPU quotas per language and trim platform CPU limits\n\nTwo changes aimed at maximizing safe concurrency on this single 4-vCPU\nnode, without adding risk of repeating the Go-style throttling failure:\n\n1. Per-language sandbox CPU quota tiers, extending the Go-only override\n   from the previous fix to every language:\n   - Python/JavaScript (pure interpretation, no compile step): 0.15\n   - Java/TypeScript (real compile step - javac/tsc): 0.5, as cheap\n     insurance against the same class of CFS-throttling failure Go hit,\n     since both were sitting at the same 0.3 quota that broke Go\n   - C/C++ stay on the 0.3 platform default (small native compiles are\n     cheap enough that no override is warranted)\n   - Go stays at 1.0 (unchanged from the previous fix)\n\n2. Trimmed platform-namespace CPU *limits* (not requests, which are\n   unchanged and still govern scheduling): auth-service, api-gateway,\n   submission-service, problem-service 750m->500m; ai-analysis-service,\n   execution-result-service 500m->400m; user-service, solution-service\n   500m->350m. discovery-service (most mesh-critical) and\n   worker-service-go (needs its full core under real load) are\n   unchanged. This drops platform-wide limits from 6700m to 5200m\n   (167%->130% of the node''s 4000m capacity) - it doesn''t change what\n   gets scheduled, but caps how far simultaneous bursts across services\n   can stack, which is what was driving the intermittent\n   Eureka/DNS-flakiness-under-load pattern (\"works, then randomly\n   doesn''t\") reported throughout today''s session.\n\nNo ConfigMap change needed for the sandbox quota tiers - all the new\ndefaults already apply.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0149o5QZBdtHxkX8gdsNfEwW\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEZwy3sG\n26jhjXLNImIzxrrMaMEq168yUnu7qq5yQRN1UKcJHN8dV9DF2K3PlSXEh7ZpLmxyWH20nee5tz3E\nYww=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-06T19:05:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/commit/b538b9563f81e24f1f80311de9a8d3473760f852","node_id":"C_kwDORTK7XtoAKGI1MzhiOTU2M2Y4MWUyNGYxZjgwMzExZGU5YThkMzQ3Mzc2MGY4NTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/commit/ac1bc14886c4a9d6486e27b90dbfdfd151acaeba","sha":"ac1bc14886c4a9d6486e27b90dbfdfd151acaeba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/commits/ac1bc14886c4a9d6486e27b90dbfdfd151acaeba"}],"sha":"b538b9563f81e24f1f80311de9a8d3473760f852","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/commits/b538b9563f81e24f1f80311de9a8d3473760f852"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90844573?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NIkhilSaravade/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NIkhilSaravade/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NIkhilSaravade/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NIkhilSaravade/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NIkhilSaravade","id":90844573,"login":"NIkhilSaravade","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwODQ0NTcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NIkhilSaravade/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NIkhilSaravade/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NIkhilSaravade/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NIkhilSaravade/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NIkhilSaravade/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.gi