ps://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/commit/27397958fed608366f5da45d68de3b35e26f74bd","node_id":"C_kwDORTK7XtoAKDI3Mzk3OTU4ZmVkNjA4MzY2ZjVkYTQ1ZDY4ZGUzYjM1ZTI2Zjc0YmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/commit/632db0eed40000d1b88b7f8748888c050db5847c","sha":"632db0eed40000d1b88b7f8748888c050db5847c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/commits/632db0eed40000d1b88b7f8748888c050db5847c"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/commit/a9dde5e582adf644a6b07d5c1ac2f4cba9201846","sha":"a9dde5e582adf644a6b07d5c1ac2f4cba9201846","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/commits/a9dde5e582adf644a6b07d5c1ac2f4cba9201846"}],"sha":"27397958fed608366f5da45d68de3b35e26f74bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/commits/27397958fed608366f5da45d68de3b35e26f74bd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/commits/a9dde5e582adf644a6b07d5c1ac2f4cba9201846/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T14:49:46Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T14:49:46Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Stop logging users out on transient network failures during token refresh\n\nrefreshAccessToken() treated ANY failure identically - a genuinely\nexpired/revoked refresh token AND a transient infra hiccup (Eureka/DNS\ncache-refresh failure, a stale pod IP producing NoRouteToHostException,\na 5xx from the gateway while the mesh reconverges) both called\nclearTokens() and logged the user out. On this single 4-vCPU node,\nthose hiccups happen every 20-30 minutes, which lines up exactly with\nusers reporting they get bounced to /login every few submissions even\nthough their session was never actually invalid.\n\nNow refreshAccessToken() only clears the session on a genuine 401/403\nfrom auth-service (the token was actually evaluated and rejected).\nNetwork-level failures and other non-2xx responses are retried a few\ntimes with a short backoff, and only rejected (without touching the\nstored tokens) if every retry fails - the session survives, and the\nnext attempt (either the proactive timer''s own retry loop, added here,\nor apiFetch''s existing reactive 401 fallback) can succeed once the\nblip passes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0149o5QZBdtHxkX8gdsNfEwW","tree":{"sha":"ece07e67e2c9b8d4bdafb25bc181fafac96158f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/git/trees/ece07e67e2c9b8d4bdafb25bc181fafac96158f8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/git/commits/a9dde5e582adf644a6b07d5c1ac2f4cba9201846","verification":{"payload":"tree ece07e67e2c9b8d4bdafb25bc181fafac96158f8\nparent 953158d157d32ad91514a8d95dc298e228ebbcd2\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1788706186 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1788706186 +0000\n\nStop logging users out on transient network failures during token refresh\n\nrefreshAccessToken() treated ANY failure identically - a genuinely\nexpired/revoked refresh token AND a transient infra hiccup (Eureka/DNS\ncache-refresh failure, a stale pod IP producing NoRouteToHostException,\na 5xx from the gateway while the mesh reconverges) both called\nclearTokens() and logged the user out. On this single 4-vCPU node,\nthose hiccups happen every 20-30 minutes, which lines up exactly with\nusers reporting they get bounced to /login every few submissions even\nthough their session was never actually invalid.\n\nNow refreshAccessToken() only clears the session on a genuine 401/403\nfrom auth-service (the token was actually evaluated and rejected).\nNetwork-level failures and other non-2xx responses are retried a few\ntimes with a short backoff, and only rejected (without touching the\nstored tokens) if every retry fails - the session survives, and the\nnext attempt (either the proactive timer''s own retry loop, added here,\nor apiFetch''s existing reactive 401 fallback) can succeed once the\nblip passes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0149o5QZBdtHxkX8gdsNfEwW\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFvQ/grq\nWT+dbj01bRNY3PVrD3UjF8wAPysDhldIrBGvhmutvt/Ar/kt/V16/K3CWWhZLcc88ei+dat1zg2s\ncAk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-06T14:49:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/commit/a9dde5e582adf644a6b07d5c1ac2f4cba9201846","node_id":"C_kwDORTK7XtoAKGE5ZGRlNWU1ODJhZGY2NDRhNmIwN2Q1YzFhYzJmNGNiYTkyMDE4NDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/commit/953158d157d32ad91514a8d95dc298e228ebbcd2","sha":"953158d157d32ad91514a8d95dc298e228ebbcd2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/commits/953158d157d32ad91514a8d95dc298e228ebbcd2"}],"sha":"a9dde5e582adf644a6b07d5c1ac2f4cba9201846","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/commits/a9dde5e582adf644a6b07d5c1ac2f4cba9201846"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/commits/953158d157d32ad91514a8d95dc298e228ebbcd2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T14:41:24Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T14:41:24Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Fix Go compile failure: GOTMPDIR directory never created\n\nPR #29 redirected GOCACHE/GOTMPDIR/HOME off the tiny 64Mi /tmp tmpfs\nonto /sandbox, but GOTMPDIR must already exist as a directory - unlike\nGOCACHE, Go''s toolchain only stats it, never creates it. Every Go\nsubmission after that fix failed at the compile step with:\n\n  go: creating work dir: stat /sandbox/.gotmp: no such file or directory\n\nRoute the compile command through a shell so mkdir -p can create both\n/sandbox/.gocache and /sandbox/.gotmp before go build runs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0149o5QZBdtHxkX8gdsNfEwW","tree":{"sha":"1fd8734c1b0ae33126e2de1c450ba79889b88359","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/git/trees/1fd8734c1b0ae33126e2de1c450ba79889b88359"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/git/commits/953158d157d32ad91514a8d95dc298e228ebbcd2","verification":{"payload":"tree 1fd8734c1b0ae33126e2de1c450ba79889b88359\nparent 632db0eed40000d1b88b7f8748888c050db5847c\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1788705684 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1788705684 +0000\n\nFix Go compile failure: GOTMPDIR directory never created\n\nPR #29 redirected GOCACHE/GOTMPDIR/HOME off the tiny 64Mi /tmp tmpfs\nonto /sandbox, but GOTMPDIR must already exist as a directory - unlike\nGOCACHE, Go''s toolchain only stats it, never creates it. Every Go\nsubmission after that fix failed at the compile step with:\n\n  go: creating work dir: stat /sandbox/.gotmp: no such file or directory\n\nRoute the compile command through a shell so mkdir -p can create both\n/sandbox/.gocache and /sandbox/.gotmp before go build runs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0149o5QZBdtHxkX8gdsNfEwW\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQL6KsSZp\nlPJTYKuMRuqMRJ4dI2UZsqJ1+2UdN92Big8yFqkzg20ejMzyV+ImlSelihI6YL6JBPwVXtHmPoJ7\njwA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-06T14:41:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admi