type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/commit/39ad7a40735dc22f5b8fed36273c9e4235d711ad","node_id":"C_kwDORTK7XtoAKDM5YWQ3YTQwNzM1ZGMyMmY1YjhmZWQzNjI3M2M5ZTQyMzVkNzExYWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/commit/21287af0421ae7a64a0c96adcacd5facd8099e8d","sha":"21287af0421ae7a64a0c96adcacd5facd8099e8d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/commits/21287af0421ae7a64a0c96adcacd5facd8099e8d"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/commit/1413666a4a1be49a45e34c8c8df46abd26d7f22b","sha":"1413666a4a1be49a45e34c8c8df46abd26d7f22b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/commits/1413666a4a1be49a45e34c8c8df46abd26d7f22b"}],"sha":"39ad7a40735dc22f5b8fed36273c9e4235d711ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/commits/39ad7a40735dc22f5b8fed36273c9e4235d711ad"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/commits/1413666a4a1be49a45e34c8c8df46abd26d7f22b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T00:47:36Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T00:47:36Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Allow getcpu syscall in sandbox seccomp profile\n\nEvery Java submission was failing with verdict CE, but with an empty\ncompile output - the actual failure was the JVM itself never starting:\n\"Error occurred during initialization of VM / getcpu(2) system call not\nsupported by kernel\". This happened for both javac and java, confirmed\nby manually exec''ing into a live sandbox-java pod and reproducing it\ndirectly (ruling out -XX:-UseContainerSupport and MALLOC_ARENA_MAX=1 as\nfixes, and ruling out gVisor since these pods run under plain runc).\n\nThe pod''s custom seccomp profile (worker-service-go/docker/seccomp/\nexecution.json, provisioned by the sandbox-seccomp-provisioner\nDaemonSet) is a strict default-deny allowlist that already permitted\nsched_getaffinity but was missing getcpu - a harmless, read-only\nsyscall (just returns the calling thread''s current CPU/NUMA node) that\nthis JVM build calls during startup. The JVM''s generic \"not supported\nby kernel\" wording is what seccomp''s SCMP_ACT_ERRNO returns for any\ndenied syscall, not an actual kernel/version limitation.\n\nSeparately, this masked a real gap in worker-service-go''s own\ndiagnostics: HotSpot''s VM-init failure text goes to stdout, not\nstderr, so the compile step''s stderr-only capture (session.CompileOutput)\nrecorded nothing even though the JVM printed a very clear error message -\nfuture compile-time infra failures like this will be equally invisible\nin the execution_result row until that capture also covers stdout.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0149o5QZBdtHxkX8gdsNfEwW","tree":{"sha":"c2248ee3cb9fc0d2e93f54e051bcf17e6ea5d0fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/git/trees/c2248ee3cb9fc0d2e93f54e051bcf17e6ea5d0fb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/git/commits/1413666a4a1be49a45e34c8c8df46abd26d7f22b","verification":{"payload":"tree c2248ee3cb9fc0d2e93f54e051bcf17e6ea5d0fb\nparent b2d41d0fe5f900006d4a7b2a737a8f6c33023ac2\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1788655656 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1788655656 +0000\n\nAllow getcpu syscall in sandbox seccomp profile\n\nEvery Java submission was failing with verdict CE, but with an empty\ncompile output - the actual failure was the JVM itself never starting:\n\"Error occurred during initialization of VM / getcpu(2) system call not\nsupported by kernel\". This happened for both javac and java, confirmed\nby manually exec''ing into a live sandbox-java pod and reproducing it\ndirectly (ruling out -XX:-UseContainerSupport and MALLOC_ARENA_MAX=1 as\nfixes, and ruling out gVisor since these pods run under plain runc).\n\nThe pod''s custom seccomp profile (worker-service-go/docker/seccomp/\nexecution.json, provisioned by the sandbox-seccomp-provisioner\nDaemonSet) is a strict default-deny allowlist that already permitted\nsched_getaffinity but was missing getcpu - a harmless, read-only\nsyscall (just returns the calling thread''s current CPU/NUMA node) that\nthis JVM build calls during startup. The JVM''s generic \"not supported\nby kernel\" wording is what seccomp''s SCMP_ACT_ERRNO returns for any\ndenied syscall, not an actual kernel/version limitation.\n\nSeparately, this masked a real gap in worker-service-go''s own\ndiagnostics: HotSpot''s VM-init failure text goes to stdout, not\nstderr, so the compile step''s stderr-only capture (session.CompileOutput)\nrecorded nothing even though the JVM printed a very clear error message -\nfuture compile-time infra failures like this will be equally invisible\nin the execution_result row until that capture also covers stdout.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0149o5QZBdtHxkX8gdsNfEwW\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLcup5zc\nwUMrTGWadeQjMEX2ULrgHY7ec586L1ys8PA070C77O1oA4FiAFA3m9dLFQXN2On1JyF17MAtI2O7\nvQ8=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-06T00:47:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/commit/1413666a4a1be49a45e34c8c8df46abd26d7f22b","node_id":"C_kwDORTK7XtoAKDE0MTM2NjZhNGExYmU0OWE0NWUzNGM4YzhkZjQ2YWJkMjZkN2YyMmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/commit/b2d41d0fe5f900006d4a7b2a737a8f6c33023ac2","sha":"b2d41d0fe5f900006d4a7b2a737a8f6c33023ac2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/commits/b2d41d0fe5f900006d4a7b2a737a8f6c33023ac2"}],"sha":"1413666a4a1be49a4