aude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/commits/20f33d8b6090559290b818907a830d10fa43de04/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T23:56:09Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T23:56:12Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Add hostAliases so worker-service-go can resolve Kafka''s advertised hostname\n\nRun/Submit still timed out even after the pod started successfully -\nlogs showed \"lookup kafka on 10.43.0.10:53: no such host\" repeating on\nevery consumer group coordinator lookup. KAFKA_BROKERS (10.0.0.14, the\nVM''s IP) works fine for the initial bootstrap connection, but Kafka''s\nbroker advertises itself back to clients as \"kafka:9093\" (matches\ndocker-compose''s KAFKA_ADVERTISED_LISTENERS, which kafka-ui and\nacls.sh''s admin client on that same docker network still need) -\nkafka-go then needs to resolve that advertised hostname itself to find\nthe coordinator, and \"kafka\" isn''t a real DNS name inside the cluster.\n\nhostAliases maps it to the VM''s IP for this pod specifically (a\npod-local /etc/hosts entry), without touching the broker config every\nother docker-compose sibling still depends on.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0149o5QZBdtHxkX8gdsNfEwW","tree":{"sha":"15e6b4649155a4d80ee98c5ff5a44c6509703ef6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/git/trees/15e6b4649155a4d80ee98c5ff5a44c6509703ef6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NIkhilSaravade/MS-code-execution-platform/git/commits/20f33d8b6090559290b818907a830d10fa43de04","verification":{"payload":"tree 15e6b4649155a4d80ee98c5ff5a44c6509703ef6\nparent 007b0a3fa47de8696ccf3e23af92874c223803ba\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1788652569 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1788652572 +0000\n\nAdd hostAliases so worker-service-go can resolve Kafka''s advertised hostname\n\nRun/Submit still timed out even after the pod started successfully -\nlogs showed \"lookup kafka on 10.43.0.10:53: no such host\" repeating on\nevery consumer group coordinator lookup. KAFKA_BROKERS (10.0.0.14, the\nVM''s IP) works fine for the initial bootstrap connection, but Kafka''s\nbroker advertises itself back to clients as \"kafka:9093\" (matches\ndocker-compose''s KAFKA_ADVERTISED_LISTENERS, which kafka-ui and\nacls.sh''s admin client on that same docker network still need) -\nkafka-go then needs to resolve that advertised hostname itself to find\nthe coordinator, and \"kafka\" isn''t a real DNS name inside the cluster.\n\nhostAliases maps it to the VM''s IP for this pod specifically (a\npod-local /etc/hosts entry), without touching the broker config every\nother docker-compose sibling still depends on.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0149o5QZBdtHxkX8gdsNfEwW\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPCe2jo6\nUm7YJffy7IcYFIy4SpxO+rZPAe6matNS26F2aDd52ssHxM35yzUoP8NGh62cQH4SJPqpUr6H7rty\nYAw=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-05T23:56:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_us