b.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/scpn-control/commits/fe80db9018238feb3323f2cc474237bdc879dc0a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T05:09:28Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T05:09:28Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"message":"fix(tests): expect the launcher''s platform refusal where it comes first\n\nThe Windows test job passed 19,961 tests, the TGLF fixture digests among\nthem, and stopped at the launcher''s missing-executable test. The\nlauncher needs POSIX process groups and refuses any other platform\nbefore it looks for the executable, so on Windows the refusal reads\n\"requires POSIX\" and not \"unavailable\". The test now expects the\nrefusal the platform gives; in both cases it still asserts that no\nexecution directory was created.\n\nThe exception ledger records the line of each runtime skip in this\nmodule; the lines moved by two, so it is resealed with the same 385\nentries.\n\nVerified on Linux: the module''s tests, the ledger contract and the hooks\npass.\n\nSeat: b52b\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)","tree":{"sha":"aa8e515738dcb728a771485eeced697158618140","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/scpn-control/git/trees/aa8e515738dcb728a771485eeced697158618140"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/scpn-control/git/commits/fe80db9018238feb3323f2cc474237bdc879dc0a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers