false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/scpn-control/commits/ea50248dfd6cca7ccb4309e79b39984bdee10667/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T04:24:49Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T04:24:49Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"message":"fix: check every text file out with LF on every platform\n\nThe Windows test job passed 19,891 tests and stopped at the TGLF reader''s\nfixture: the digest of a provider output file differed from the recorded\none. The attribute policy pinned LF for listed extensions only, so a\nWindows checkout rewrote every other text file with CR LF. About 140\ntracked files fall under that rule, among them the provider outputs,\nwhich have no common extension, the requirement locks, JSON-lines\nrecords and equilibrium files, several of which are content-hashed.\n\nThe default rule now pins LF for every file git treats as text. The\nrepository''s content does not change, and neither does a checkout on\nLinux or macOS. No tracked batch or PowerShell script exists that would\nneed CR LF.\n\nVerified on Linux: the attributes resolve to LF for the fixture and a\nrequirement lock, the working tree shows no other change, and the hooks\nand the reader''s tests pass. Not verified: the Windows checkout itself,\nwhich only the hosted job shows.\n\nSeat: b52b\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)","tree":{"sha":"0930bc706050e3e11fde2fe96533699c3b009ea2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/scpn-control/git/trees/0930bc706050e3e11fde2fe96533699c3b009ea2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/scpn-control/git/commits/ea50248dfd6cca7ccb4309e79b39984bdee10667",