ubscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/scpn-control/commits/ac3d001dcac168f183cf0c46033b967f8688e81e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T19:19:02Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T19:19:02Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"message":"fix(ci): document and test relocated owners and satisfy Clippy 1.98\n\nThe push that published 67f89868, ab5e615e and 5aadfebb left four gates\nred on main. The checkpoint-integrity and fault-injector code had moved\ninto disruption_checkpoint_integrity and fault_injector while docs/api.md\nand the tests still named only the re-exporting modules, so the docs\ncoverage and untested-module guards failed; the directives now name the\nowner modules, add verified_checkpoint_snapshot, and the tests import\nfrom the owners. New tests cover the snapshot''s byte copy, immunity to\npath replacement after verification and its fail-closed refusals, and\nthe fault injector''s pass-through, dropout, drift and range contracts.\nThe transport smoothing loop iterates the solved profile instead of\nindexing it (clippy::needless_range_loop); behaviour is unchanged. The\ncapability manifest is regenerated.\n\nSeat: b52b\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)","tree":{"sha":"4d62140f76e6615c17ab2f452239aa160cc8d220","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/scpn-control/git/trees/4d62140f76e6615c17ab2f452239aa160cc8d220"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/scpn-control/git/commits/ac3d001dcac168f183cf0c46033b967f8688e81e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.